  "raw": " counterpart, the villain.\n\n\"I won't say why the die is cast.\"\n\n\"No! It matters!\" the villain shouted, pulling the die out of the air to reveal it made the familiar shape of fifty six: a large, blue star. A star shaped like that! The villain gasped, looking up at the sky and suddenly dropping his hand from Random, who didn't move.\n\nThe villain slowly reached for Random again, trying to catch him in a bear hug, but as he moved one hand, it reached out towards the sky and a great blue aura surrounded Random. Random's eyes closed and his head became heavy.\n\nThe villain raised his hand to catch him, but once his finger reached out, a great blue aura surrounded Random and suddenly there was an immense glow. He was fading!\n\nThe villain had completely faded away a moment before.",
  "serialized": "counterpart, the villain. \"I won't say why the die is cast.\" \"No! It matters!\" the villain shouted, pulling the die out of the air to reveal it made the familiar shape of fifty six: a large, blue star. A star shaped like that! The villain gasped, looking up at the sky and suddenly dropping his hand from Random, who didn't move. The villain slowly reached for Random again, trying to catch him in a bear hug, but as he moved one hand, it reached out towards the sky and a great blue aura surrounded Random. Random's eyes closed and his head became heavy. The villain raised his hand to catch him, but once his finger reached out, a great blue aura surrounded Random and suddenly there was an immense glow. He was fading! The villain had completely faded away a moment before.",
